WEBVTT

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:02.453
The when to go.

00:00:02.513 --> 00:00:08.978
A wealthy man wanted to go hunting in a part of Northern Canada where few people had ever hunted.

00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:13.131
He traveled to a trading post and tried to find a guy to take him.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.572
But no one would do it.

00:00:14.631 --> 00:00:16.612
It was too dangerous, they said.

00:00:16.672 --> 00:00:22.318
Finally, he found an Indian who needed money badly and he agreed to take him.

00:00:22.378 --> 00:00:26.081
The Indian's name was Defago.

00:00:26.141 --> 00:00:30.186
They made camp in the snow near a large frozen lake.

00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:35.170
For three days they hunted, but they had nothing to show for it.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.043
The third night a windstorm came up.

00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:44.659
They lay on their tent listening to the wind howling and the trees whipping back and forth.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:48.486
To see the storm better, the hunter opened the tent flap.

00:00:48.546 --> 00:00:51.458
What he saw started him.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:58.606
There wasn't a breath of air stirring, and the trees were standing perfectly still.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:02.260
Yet he could hear the wind howling.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:11.552
And the more he listened, the more it sounded as if it were calling to Faygo's name.

00:01:11.611 --> 00:01:19.150
I must be losing my mind the hunt of thought.

00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:23.250
But Defago had gotten out of his sleeping bag.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.092
He was huddled in a corner of the tent, his head buried in his arms.

00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:31.604
What's this all about, the hunter said?

00:01:31.664 --> 00:01:34.996
It's nothing, Defago said.

00:01:35.056 --> 00:01:45.413
But the wind continued to call to him, and Defago became more tense and more restless.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:52.650
Suddenly, he jumped to his feet and he began to run from the tent.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.883
But the hunter grabbed him and wrestled him to the ground.

00:01:55.942 --> 00:01:59.215
You can't leave me out here, the hunter shouted.

00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:05.480
Then the wind called again and the fago broke loose and ran into the darkness.

00:02:05.539 --> 00:02:09.272
The hunter could hear him screaming as he went.

00:02:09.332 --> 00:02:15.076
Again and again he cried, oh my fiery feet, my burning feet of fire.

00:02:15.136 --> 00:02:20.820
Then his voice faded away and the wind died down.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:27.102
At daybreak, the hunter followed Defago's tracks in the snow.

00:02:27.162 --> 00:02:32.717
They went through the woods down toward the lake, then out onto the ice.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:35.880
But soon he noticed something strange.

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:40.043
The steps Defago had taken got longer and longer.

00:02:40.102 --> 00:02:43.734
They were so long no human being could have taken them.

00:02:43.794 --> 00:02:47.800
It was as if something had helped him to hurry away.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:54.895
The hunter followed the tracks out to the middle of the lake, but there they disappeared.

00:02:54.954 --> 00:03:00.037
At first he thought the fago would fall into the ice, but there wasn't any hole.

00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:06.130
Then he thought something had pulled him off the ice into the sky, but that made no sense.

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:11.402
As he stood wondering what had happened, the wind picked up again.

00:03:11.462 --> 00:03:15.525
Soon it was howling as it had the night before.

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:18.057
Then he heard Defago's voice.

00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:20.178
It was coming from up above.

00:03:20.238 --> 00:03:26.359
And again he heard Defago screaming, my fiery feet, my burning feet.

00:03:26.419 --> 00:03:30.150
But there was nothing to be seen.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.901
Now the hunter wanted to leave that place as fast as he could.

00:03:34.961 --> 00:03:37.682
He went back to camp and packed.

00:03:37.742 --> 00:03:41.943
Then he left some food for Defago and he started out.

00:03:42.002 --> 00:03:45.996
Weeks later he reached civilization.

00:03:46.056 --> 00:03:50.164
The following year he went back to hunt in that area again.

00:03:50.224 --> 00:03:53.688
He went to the same trading post to look for a guide.

00:03:53.748 --> 00:04:00.496
The people there could not explain what had happened to Defago that night, but they had not seen him since then.

00:04:00.556 --> 00:04:05.841
Maybe it was the windigo, one of them said, and he laughed.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.710
It's supposed to come up with the wind.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:13.748
It drags you along at great speed until your feet are burned away and more of you than that.

00:04:13.808 --> 00:04:16.678
Then it carries you into the sky and it drops you.

00:04:16.738 --> 00:04:18.479
It's just a crazy story.

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:21.220
But that's what some of the Indians say.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.221
A few days later the hunter was at the trading post again.

00:04:25.281 --> 00:04:28.492
An Indian came in and sat by the fire.

00:04:28.552 --> 00:04:33.804
He had a blanket wrapped around him and he wore his hat so that you couldn't see his face.

00:04:33.864 --> 00:04:37.686
The hunter thought there was something familiar about him.

00:04:37.746 --> 00:04:42.590
He walked over and he asked, are you Defago?

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:46.162
The Indian didn't answer.

00:04:46.222 --> 00:04:49.524
Do you know anything about him?

00:04:49.584 --> 00:04:52.225
No answer.

00:04:52.284 --> 00:05:00.600
He began to wonder if something was wrong, if the man needed help, but he couldn't see his face.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.641
Are you all right, he asked?

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.294
No answer.

00:05:07.354 --> 00:05:12.361
To get a look at him, he lifted the Indian's hat.

00:05:12.421 --> 00:05:15.694
Then he screamed.

00:05:15.754 --> 00:05:23.217
There was nothing under the hat but a pile of ashes.

00:05:23.277 --> 00:06:00.724
Some people say a man is made out of mud A bone man's made out of muscle and blood Muscle and blood and skin and bones A mind that's weak and a back that's strong you load 16 tons Why do you get another day older and deeper in depth St Peter don't you call me cause I can't go I owe my soul to the company store Such things happen.

00:06:00.784 --> 00:06:07.957
When Bill Nilsen's cow stopped giving milk, he called the veterinarian.

00:06:08.017 --> 00:06:12.490
There's nothing wrong with that cow, the vet said.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.542
She's just stubborn.

00:06:14.602 --> 00:06:17.602
That or some witch got hold of her.

00:06:17.662 --> 00:06:20.500
Bill and the vet both laughed.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.007
That old hag, Addy Fitch.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:26.858
I guess she's the closest we've got to a witch around here, though, that said.

00:06:26.918 --> 00:06:30.370
But witches have gone out of style, haven't they?

00:06:30.429 --> 00:06:34.802
Bill had had a running with Addy Fitch the month before.

00:06:34.862 --> 00:06:40.454
He had hit her cat with his car and killed it.

00:06:40.514 --> 00:06:45.456
I'm really sorry, Addy Fitch, he told her.

00:06:45.516 --> 00:06:49.844
I'll get you a new cat, just as pretty, just as good.

00:06:49.904 --> 00:06:52.992
Her eyes filled with hate.

00:06:53.052 --> 00:06:56.704
I raised that cat from a kitten, she hissed.

00:06:56.764 --> 00:06:58.076
I loved her.

00:06:58.136 --> 00:07:01.238
You'll be sorry for this, Bill Nelson.

00:07:01.298 --> 00:07:05.952
Bill sent her a new cat and heard nothing more.

00:07:06.012 --> 00:07:10.426
Then his cow stopped giving milk.

00:07:10.486 --> 00:07:14.248
Next, his old truck broke down.

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:18.692
After that, his wife fell and broke her arm.

00:07:18.752 --> 00:07:21.513
We're having a lot of bad luck, he thought.

00:07:21.573 --> 00:07:25.404
Then he thought, maybe it's Addy Fitch getting even.

00:07:25.464 --> 00:07:31.236
And then, hey, you don't believe in witches, you're just upset.

00:07:31.296 --> 00:07:34.576
But Bill's grandpa believed in witches.

00:07:34.636 --> 00:07:40.040
He had once told Bill that there was only one sure way to stop a witch from causing trouble.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.354
You find a black walnut tree," he said.

00:07:43.414 --> 00:07:51.290
And you draw a picture on it, then you mark an X where her heart is, and you drive a nail into the X.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:55.394
Every day you drive it in a little deeper.

00:07:55.454 --> 00:07:59.498
If she's causing the trouble, he said, she'll feel the pain.

00:07:59.558 --> 00:08:05.792
When she can't stand it anymore, she'll come to you or send somebody and try to borrow something.

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:12.475
If you give her what she wants, that breaks the power of the nail, and she'll go on tormenting you.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:19.210
But if you don't, she'll have to stop, or the pain will kill her."

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:25.044
That's what his nice gentle old grandpa believed, his pure craziness bill thought.

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:28.476
Of course, his grandpa didn't have much schooling.

00:08:28.536 --> 00:08:31.960
Bill had been to college, and he knew better.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:40.097
Then Bill's dog Joe, a perfectly healthy dog, dropped dead, just like that.

00:08:40.157 --> 00:08:43.079
It made Bill angry.

00:08:43.139 --> 00:08:49.994
Despite all his schooling he thought, maybe it is Addy Fitch after all.

00:08:50.054 --> 00:08:58.750
He got a red crayon from his son's room, and a hammer, and a nail, and went him to the woods.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:04.712
He found a black walnut tree and drew a picture of Addie Fitch on it.

00:09:04.772 --> 00:09:11.976
He marked an X where her heart was, like his grandpa had said to do.

00:09:12.036 --> 00:09:15.787
With the hammer he drove the nail a little way into the X.

00:09:15.847 --> 00:09:17.767
Then he went home.

00:09:17.828 --> 00:09:20.149
I feel like a fool, he told his wife.

00:09:20.209 --> 00:09:22.650
You should, she said.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:26.661
The next day a boy named Timmy Logan came by.

00:09:26.722 --> 00:09:30.620
Addie Fitch isn't feeling well, he said.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:35.001
She wondered as if she could borrow some sugar from you.

00:09:35.061 --> 00:09:39.394
Bill Nelson stared at Timmy in amazement.

00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:42.486
He took a deep breath.

00:09:42.546 --> 00:09:49.462
Tell her I'm sorry, but I don't have any sugar right now, he said.

00:09:49.522 --> 00:09:58.314
When Timmy Logan left, Bill went back to the walnut tree and drove the nail in another inch.

00:09:58.374 --> 00:10:02.174
The next day, the boy came back.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:05.606
Addy Fritch is pretty sick, he said.

00:10:05.666 --> 00:10:09.548
She's wondering if you've got any sugar yet.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:15.430
Tell her I'm sorry Bill Nelson said, but I still don't have any.

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:21.834
Bill went out into the woods and drove the nail in another inch.

00:10:21.894 --> 00:10:26.185
The following day, the boy was back.

00:10:26.244 --> 00:10:29.194
Addy Fitch is getting sicker, he said.

00:10:29.254 --> 00:10:31.786
She really needs some sugar.

00:10:31.846 --> 00:10:35.999
Tell her I still don't have any, Bill answered.

00:10:36.059 --> 00:10:38.721
Bill's wife was angry.

00:10:38.781 --> 00:10:41.262
You've got to stop this, she said.

00:10:41.322 --> 00:10:45.356
If this mumbo-jumbo works, it's like murder.

00:10:45.416 --> 00:10:49.228
I'll stop when she does, he said.

00:10:49.288 --> 00:10:57.188
Toward dusk, he stood in the yard staring at the ridge where the old lady lived, wondering what was going on up there.

00:10:57.248 --> 00:11:03.198
Then in the half-darkness, he saw Addy Fitch coming slowly down the hill toward him.

00:11:03.258 --> 00:11:08.672
With her pinched bony face and her all-black coat, she did look like a witch.

00:11:08.732 --> 00:11:14.386
As she got closer, Bill saw that she could hardly walk.

00:11:14.446 --> 00:11:17.728
Maybe I'm really hurting her, he thought.

00:11:17.788 --> 00:11:26.804
He ran to get his hammer to pull the nail out, but before he could leave, Addy Fitch was in the yard, her face twisted with rage.

00:11:26.864 --> 00:11:30.637
First you killed my cat, she said.

00:11:30.696 --> 00:11:34.079
Then you wouldn't give me a bit of sugar when I needed it.

00:11:34.139 --> 00:11:36.220
She swore at him.

00:11:36.281 --> 00:11:41.004
And fell dead at his feet.

00:11:41.064 --> 00:11:46.990
I'm not surprised that she dropped dead that way, the doctor said later.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.671
She was very old, maybe 90.

00:11:49.731 --> 00:11:51.723
It was her heart, of course.

00:11:51.783 --> 00:11:55.016
Some people thought she was a witch, Bill said.

00:11:55.076 --> 00:11:57.767
I've heard that, the doctor said.

00:11:57.827 --> 00:12:01.920
Somebody I know thought Addie Fitchard wished him, Bill went on.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:06.884
He drew a picture of her on a tree, then drove a nail into it to make her stop.

00:12:06.944 --> 00:12:10.076
That's old superstition, the doctor said.

00:12:10.136 --> 00:12:15.910
But people like us don't believe in that sort of thing, do we?

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:22.406
I don't take no limb in this cannon on my hip.

00:12:22.466 --> 00:12:26.031
Let me tell you boy, ain't no toy.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:41.908
Is something wrong?

00:12:41.968 --> 00:12:59.704
A car broke down late at night way out in the country.

00:12:59.764 --> 00:13:03.587
The driver remembered passing an empty house a few minutes earlier.

00:13:03.647 --> 00:13:05.438
I'll stay there, he thought.

00:13:05.498 --> 00:13:08.030
At least I'll get some sleep.

00:13:08.089 --> 00:13:13.022
He found some wood in the corner of the living room and made a fire in the fireplace.

00:13:13.082 --> 00:13:15.854
He covered himself with his coat and slept.

00:13:15.914 --> 00:13:19.966
Toward morning the fire went out and the cold awakened him.

00:13:20.026 --> 00:13:22.278
It'll be light soon, he thought.

00:13:22.338 --> 00:13:24.260
Then I'll go for help.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:30.599
He closed his eyes again, but before he could doze off there was a terrible crash.

00:13:30.659 --> 00:13:35.676
Something big and heavy had fallen out of the chimney.

00:13:35.736 --> 00:13:37.988
It lay on the floor for a minute.

00:13:38.048 --> 00:13:41.394
Then it stood up and stared down on him.

00:13:41.454 --> 00:13:44.598
The man took one look and started running.

00:13:44.658 --> 00:13:47.830
He'd never seen anything so horrible in his life.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.882
He paused just long enough to jump through a window.

00:13:50.942 --> 00:13:58.226
Then he ran and ran and ran and ran until he thought his lungs would burst.

00:13:58.286 --> 00:14:04.229
As he stood in the road panting, trying to catch his breath, he felt something tap him on the shoulder.

00:14:04.289 --> 00:14:10.460
He turned and found himself staring into two big bloody eyes in a grinning skull.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.470
It was a horrible thing.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:28.030
Part of me, it said, is something wrong.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:54.603
Hi Beams!

00:14:54.663 --> 00:15:12.642
The girl driving the old blue Sudan was a senior at the high school.

00:15:12.702 --> 00:15:17.976
She lived on a farm about eight miles away and used the car to drive back and forth.

00:15:18.036 --> 00:15:21.808
She had driven into town that night to see a baseball game.

00:15:21.868 --> 00:15:24.100
Now she was on her way home.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:29.784
As she pulled away from the school she noticed a red pickup truck follow her out of the parking lot.

00:15:29.844 --> 00:15:33.257
A few minutes later the truck was still behind her.

00:15:33.317 --> 00:15:36.938
I guess we're going in the same direction she thought.

00:15:36.998 --> 00:15:40.518
She began to watch the truck in her mirror.

00:15:40.579 --> 00:15:45.060
When she changed speed, the driver of the truck changed his speed.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:49.001
When she passed a car, so did he.

00:15:49.061 --> 00:15:55.812
Then he turned on his high beams, flooding her car with light.

00:15:55.872 --> 00:15:58.974
He left them on for almost a minute.

00:15:59.034 --> 00:16:02.274
He probably wants to pass me, she thought.

00:16:02.334 --> 00:16:05.678
But she was becoming uneasy.

00:16:05.738 --> 00:16:09.431
Usually she drove home over a back road.

00:16:09.491 --> 00:16:12.352
Not too many people went that way.

00:16:12.412 --> 00:16:18.314
But when she turned onto that road, so did the truck.

00:16:18.374 --> 00:16:21.425
I've got to get away from him, she thought.

00:16:21.485 --> 00:16:23.826
And she began to drive faster.

00:16:23.886 --> 00:16:27.227
Then he turned his high beams on again.

00:16:27.287 --> 00:16:30.878
After a minute, he turned them off.

00:16:30.938 --> 00:16:34.408
Then he turned them on again, and off again.

00:16:34.468 --> 00:16:39.860
She drove even faster, but the truck stayed right behind her.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:43.672
Then he turned his high beams on again.

00:16:43.732 --> 00:16:46.604
Once more, her car was ablaze with light.

00:16:46.664 --> 00:16:48.586
What is he doing, she wondered?

00:16:48.646 --> 00:16:50.466
What does he want?

00:16:50.526 --> 00:16:52.928
Then he turned them off again.

00:16:52.988 --> 00:16:59.324
But a minute later, he had them on again, and he left them on.

00:16:59.384 --> 00:17:05.109
At last she pulled into her driveway and the truck pulled right in behind her.

00:17:05.169 --> 00:17:07.880
She jumped from the car and ran to the house.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:09.230
Call the police!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.031
She screamed at her father.

00:17:11.091 --> 00:17:14.453
Out in the driveway she could see the driver of the truck.

00:17:14.512 --> 00:17:20.966
He had a gun in his hand.

00:17:21.026 --> 00:17:29.731
When the police arrived, they started to arrest him, but he pointed to the girl's car.

00:17:29.791 --> 00:17:31.022
You don't want me, he said.

00:17:31.082 --> 00:17:32.592
You want him!

00:17:32.653 --> 00:17:38.937
Crouched behind the driver's seat, there was a man with a knife.

00:17:38.997 --> 00:17:45.442
As the driver of the truck explained it, the man slipped into the girl's car before she left the school.

00:17:45.502 --> 00:17:49.794
He saw it happen, but there was no way he could stop it.

00:17:49.855 --> 00:17:55.956
He thought about getting the police, but he was afraid to leave her, so he followed her car.

00:17:56.016 --> 00:18:03.097
Each time the man in the backseat reached up to overpower her, the driver of the truck turned on his high beams.

00:18:03.157 --> 00:18:14.036
Then the man dropped down, afraid that somebody might see him.

00:18:14.096 --> 00:18:51.334
Not to Alaska, or North, or North, or North, or North, or North, or North, or North, or North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North, North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North North bed by the window.

00:18:51.394 --> 00:19:06.552
Three old men shared a room at the nursing home.

00:19:06.613 --> 00:19:23.421
The room had only one window, but for them it was the only link to the real world.

00:19:23.481 --> 00:19:28.534
Ted Conklin, who had been there the longest, had the bed next to the window.

00:19:28.594 --> 00:19:36.117
When Ted died, the man in the next bed, George Best took his place, and the third man, Richard Green, took George's bed.

00:19:36.177 --> 00:19:42.802
Despite his illness, George was a cheerful man who spent his days describing the sights he could see from his bed.

00:19:42.862 --> 00:19:51.632
Pretty girls, a policeman on horseback, a traffic jam, a pizza parlor, a fire station, and other scenes of life outside.

00:19:51.692 --> 00:19:58.802
Richard loved to listen to George, but the more George talked about life outside, the more Richard wanted to see it for himself.

00:19:58.862 --> 00:20:03.406
Yet he knew that only when George died would he have his chance.

00:20:03.466 --> 00:20:09.272
He wanted to look out that window so badly that one day he decided to kill George.

00:20:09.332 --> 00:20:14.496
He's going to die soon anyway, he told himself, what difference does it make?

00:20:14.556 --> 00:20:17.226
George had a bad heart.

00:20:17.286 --> 00:20:23.219
If he had an attack during the night and the nurse could not get to him right away, he had pills he could take.

00:20:23.279 --> 00:20:27.471
He kept them in a bottle on top of the cabinet between his bed and Richards.

00:20:27.531 --> 00:20:32.789
All Richard had to do was knock the bottle to the floor when George could not reach it.

00:20:32.849 --> 00:20:37.436
A few nights later, George died just as Richard had planned he would.

00:20:37.496 --> 00:20:41.276
And the next morning, Richard was moved to the bed by the window.

00:20:41.336 --> 00:20:47.038
Now he would see for himself all the things outside that George had described.

00:20:47.098 --> 00:20:52.479
